# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
!coverage.go
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file (secrets; change .env-example instead) and the local private-module token
.env
.go_private_token

# Build outputs (make build writes bin/; make cover-all writes .coverage/)
bin/
.coverage/
# Root-anchored: a bare `server` (no leading slash) would also match the
# cmd/server/ *directory* at any depth and silently hide real source files.
# These match only root-level binaries from `go build ./cmd/<name>` run
# without -o from the repo root (never commit binaries; use make build).
/server
/jobs
/migrate
/certify
/commercial-billing

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
.vscode/

# Claude Code agent worktrees (temporary, not project code)
.claude/worktrees/

# Staged Glue schema copies under their event-type names (make _stage-produced / schema-register, CI)
.tmp/
